DCE Clock-Rate Removal Check (Packet Tracer Serial0/0/0):
  - Removing 'clock rate 64000' on R1 (DCE) stops clocking pulses -> Serial0/0/0 status becomes 'up/down' (line protocol down),
    causing the primary static route to be withdrawn and traffic to fail over to the AD 200 floating static route.

--- Alternative Concept Analysis: Static Routes vs OSPF ---
  - 2 Campuses  : Static+Floating = ~4 route lines; OSPF = ~6 lines (comparable).
  - 5 Campuses  : Full-mesh static routes need ~5 x 4 x 2 (primary+backup) = 40+ manual lines;
                  OSPF needs ~5 lines/router regardless of remote prefixes.
  - Failover    : Floating static fails over instantly ONLY if link-down detected; fails to detect mid-path failure without IP SLA.
                  OSPF detects link-down (<1 s carrier) or Hello dead timer (40 s default, <200 ms with BFD) end-to-end.
